Upstream-Status: Pending
Exit: Drop when freedesktop-sdk's python3-setuptools-scm.bst upstream carries ref-format: git-describe on its git_repo source.
Subject: python3-setuptools-scm: stage tag refs so sandbox git-describe returns

The git_repo source currently relies on the default ref-format (sha1).
Under that mode the plugin does not guarantee tag refs are present in
the sandbox clone. setuptools-scm's build hook runs

    git describe --dirty --tags --long --abbrev=40 --match 'setuptools-scm-*'

which has to walk the commit graph looking for a matching tag; with no
tag refs it exhausts setuptools-scm's default 40-second subprocess
timeout and fails the build (subprocess.TimeoutExpired).

Setting ref-format: git-describe instructs the plugin to stage the tag
refs so the sandbox git-describe returns in milliseconds. The element's
existing ref (setuptools-scm-v10.3.4-0-gb27f5973...) is already in
git-describe format, so this is consistent with how the ref is stored.

Resolves: setuptools-scm#957 (upstream has since made TimeoutExpired
non-fatal, but ref-format is the structural fix.)

diff --git a/elements/components/python3-setuptools-scm.bst b/elements/components/python3-setuptools-scm.bst
--- a/elements/components/python3-setuptools-scm.bst
+++ b/elements/components/python3-setuptools-scm.bst
@@ -21,6 +21,7 @@ variables:
 sources:
 - kind: git_repo
   url: github:pypa/setuptools_scm.git
+  ref-format: git-describe
   track: setuptools-scm-v*
   exclude:
   - "*dev*"
